cff-version: 1.2.0
message: "If you use exostab, please cite it as below, together with the methods and data it relies on (see docs/references.bib)."
title: "exostab: honest, traceable orbital-stability indicators for known exoplanet systems"
abstract: >-
  exostab reports whether a known multi-planet system is dynamically stable using three indicators:
  Hill spacing, the angular momentum deficit, and direct N-body integration with the MEGNO chaos
  indicator, with parameters from the NASA Exoplanet Archive and every data assumption recorded.
type: software
